                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For truck owners and fleet managers, downtime isn't just inconvenient; it's expensive. A single truck sitting in the yard can mean missed deliveries, unhappy customers, and lost revenue.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "That's why truck PM service (preventive maintenance service) is one of the most important investments you can make in your equipment. Preventive maintenance helps catch small problems before they become major repairs. Instead of reacting to breakdowns on the road, a scheduled PM service keeps your vehicles running reliably day after day. For owner-operators and fleet managers alike, consistent maintenance is the difference between running smoothly and constantly playing catch-up.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-what-is-pm",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Is a Truck PM Service?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "what-is-pm"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-is-pm-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A truck PM service is a scheduled preventive maintenance visit designed to keep your truck operating safely and efficiently. Rather than waiting for something to fail, technicians inspect key systems, replace worn components, and ensure the truck is ready for the road. At Sun State International, the goal of PM service is simple: keep your truck working as hard as you do. Because when your truck is running reliably, your business can keep moving forward.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
